# rd_fixture_helpers.cmake: what a -P test script calls to replay the committed
# fixtures (docs/port/TESTING_FIXTURES.md).  The script is given
#   -DFIXTURE_TOOL=<rd_fixture_tool> -DFIXTURES=<port/render/test/fixtures>
# and includes this file (-DFIXTURE_HELPERS=<this file>).
#
#   rd_fixture_list(LIST OUT)
#       the fixture names a list names, in order (a name a line, '#'
#       comments; the words after a name are kept in RDFX_FIELDS_<name>); a
#       line that is a path (a '/', a '\', '..', ':') FAILS: a test reads
#       nothing from outside the repository
#   rd_fixture_expand(NAME DIR OUT)
#       FIXTURES/NAME.rdfix expanded into DIR/NAME.rddump (in the build
#       tree, never committed), its SHA-256 checked by the tool; OUT the
#       dump's path.  A listed fixture that is absent or does not expand
#       to its pin FAILS
#   rd_fixture_require(NAME TEXT QUANTITY...)
#       the path ran: every property the fixture declares (expect=, the
#       tool's props) whose quantity is one of QUANTITY is checked against
#       TEXT (a replay's --stats output); a property that does not hold, a
#       quantity TEXT does not show, or a fixture that declares none of the
#       QUANTITYs is an error (SEND_ERROR), counted in RDFX_FAILURES
#   rd_fixture_quantity(NAME TEXT OUT)
#       one quantity's value in TEXT ("" when TEXT does not show it)
#
# The quantities (each the first match of its regex in the --stats lines,
# rd_replay_tool's words; add a row for a new property):
